WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.182 --> 00:00:05.463
miR-Target predicts the genes a miRNA targets with several tools, and shows where the tools agree.

2
00:00:05.463 --> 00:00:18.006
Step 1: choose the species. For human, also choose the genome reference; we use hg38.

3
00:00:18.006 --> 00:00:30.096
Step 2: pick the miRNA from the catalog. Type part of its name to filter.

4
00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:36.304
The summary shows the mature sequence and where it sits on its precursor.

5
00:00:36.304 --> 00:00:42.857
Or choose Custom Sequence to paste your own mature sequence (17–30 nt).

6
00:00:42.857 --> 00:00:49.505
Step 3 (optional): shift the mature sequence along its precursor, or change single bases.

7
00:00:49.505 --> 00:01:04.140
Each variant is predicted alongside the wild type and can be compared with it. We keep the wild type here.

8
00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:16.048
Step 4: choose the prediction tools. More tools give a stronger consensus.

9
00:01:16.048 --> 00:01:25.917
To keep this example quick we choose four. RNAhybrid takes the longest on a genome-wide run.

10
00:01:25.917 --> 00:01:33.441
Step 5: optionally limit predictions to genes you name. We predict genome-wide, which enrichment needs.

11
00:01:33.441 --> 00:01:40.175
Step 6: review the job, then start it.

12
00:01:40.175 --> 00:01:47.616
The job runs in the background and shows each tool's progress. Keep this page's link to come back.
